# Coverage exclusions (SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only)
# One entry per line: <area>: <pattern> | <reason>. area = swift (regex on the file path), pwa (glob as in
# pwa/vite.config.ts coverage.exclude; scripts/coverage-ratchet.sh checks both lists are identical) or php (regex on the path).
# Every exclusion needs a reason; an entry without one makes the check fail. Do not exclude code merely because it is untested:
# untested code belongs in the baseline (scripts/coverage-baseline.json), not here.
swift: /\.build/ | Checked-out dependencies and generated build files, not our code.
swift: /Vendor/ | Vendored third-party code; covered by its own upstream tests.
swift: /Tests/ | Test code itself must not count towards the product coverage.
swift: /Sources/App/main\.swift$ | Executable entry point (process bootstrap, signal handling); exercised only by the real end-to-end runs.
pwa: src/**/*.test.ts | Test code itself.
pwa: src/**/*.d.ts | Type declarations only, no executable code.
pwa: src/test-setup.ts | Test harness setup.
pwa: src/main.ts | Application bootstrap (mounts the root component into the document); covered by the Playwright specs.
php: /tests/ | Test scripts themselves.
